1
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:06,100
How sleazy. I want some kimchi.

2
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:06,430
Muhyeok! Muhyeok!

3
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:08,730
Muhyeok! Muhyeok!

4
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,960
Muhyeok! Muhyeok!

5
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:16,760
Muhyeok! Get up!

6
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:17,990
Muhyeok!

7
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,900
Muhyeok!

8
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:43,819
[Episode 2]

9
00:01:43,819 --> 00:01:45,387
[Choi Yun's Concert
- Special Offline Meetup]

10
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:38,260
Is Choi Yun's stylist coordinator in here?

11
00:02:39,210 --> 00:02:41,880
Excuse me, aren't you Choi Yun's coordinator?

12
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:44,270
- Yes. Me?
- Choi Yun is done singing.

13
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:45,310
Okay.

14
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:07,610
This lady right next to me...
Everyone knows who she is, right?

15
00:03:07,610 --> 00:03:09,160
Yes!

16
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:17,830
She has always been my idol...

17
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:21,300
She is my rival who I can never beat.

18
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,500
She is the one who always makes me happy.

19
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,370
My mother.

20
00:03:31,130 --> 00:03:36,930
Everyone remembers my mom
as one of the greatest movie stars,

21
00:03:36,930 --> 00:03:41,590
but her dream has always been
to become a singer, like me.

22
00:03:43,350 --> 00:03:46,750
When I was stressed and exhausted,

23
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:51,830
she always sang me a certain song
with my head upon her lap.

24
00:03:51,830 --> 00:03:56,810
Today, I would like to share that song with everyone.

25
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:24,130
Muhyeok!

26
00:05:24,130 --> 00:05:25,750
Muhyeok! Don't leave me like this!

27
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,300
Wake up!

28
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:36,540
Muhyeok!

29
00:05:37,650 --> 00:05:39,020
Muhyeok!

30
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,240
Don't leave me!

31
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:14,050
Muhyeok!

32
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:13,556
I'm afraid two stray bullets are lodged in his skull.

33
00:07:13,556 --> 00:07:17,014
We removed the bullet lodged
in the left brain hemisphere,

34
00:07:17,014 --> 00:07:22,310
but the one in the afterbrain, I'm afraid it was just
too risky for us to operate on that one.

35
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:27,866
The risk of him dying from surgery was way too high,
so we had to leave it there.

36
00:07:44,356 --> 00:07:54,834
It was miracle enough that he escaped death,
but we can't be sure how long he'll be able to live.

37
00:08:16,793 --> 00:08:21,310
When he wakes up, he may experience changes
in character and personality

38
00:08:21,310 --> 00:08:25,137
because his left brain has been damaged.

39
00:08:25,452 --> 00:08:34,128
He may feel nervous at times or even become violent.

40
00:08:35,045 --> 00:08:38,041
What kind of person was he before?

41
00:10:22,610 --> 00:10:25,100
No, Muhyeok. No!

42
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:05,050
They said you need rest.

43
00:11:05,050 --> 00:11:06,900
You're not normal.

44
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:14,230
There's still a bullet in your head.

45
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:18,220
Didn't the doctor tell you?

46
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,320
Muhyeok!

47
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:27,050
You're back, right?

48
00:11:29,470 --> 00:11:31,900
I knew you'd be back.

49
00:11:33,090 --> 00:11:34,750
I knew you would.

50
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,570
Go to Korea.

51
00:11:44,390 --> 00:11:46,310
I got you a ticket, packed some clothes,

52
00:11:46,310 --> 00:11:49,450
and enough money to last you a lifetime.

53
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:55,160
Leave. Your flight's tonight.

54
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:03,010
If you go home, you'll die.

55
00:12:03,010 --> 00:12:04,950
Jason is trying to kill you.

56
00:12:04,950 --> 00:12:07,300
Jason was the one who sent that car.

57
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:11,110
He probably burned your house down.

58
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:22,210
I'm sorry, Muhyeok. This is all I have to give.

59
00:12:23,110 --> 00:12:26,550
You saved our lives,

60
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:29,930
but I'm so sorry this is all I have to give.

61
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:34,890
If he wants me dead, I guess I'll just die.

62
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,230
If you want to die, die in Korea.

63
00:12:38,230 --> 00:12:43,880
Don't die here like a dog, go back and end it there.

64
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,800
Am I dying?

65
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:51,110
We'll soon be landing in Incheon International Airport.

66
00:13:51,110 --> 00:13:56,130
We hope you make beautiful memories in Seoul,

67
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:57,550
the city of hope and love. Thank you.

68
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:09,530
Poison.

69
00:14:09,530 --> 00:14:12,640
You took this and died, didn't you?

70
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,570
Oh, careless love!

71
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:19,380
Why didn't you leave me a single drop?

72
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,510
Oh, dagger...

73
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:26,670
Let my heart be its sheath.

74
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:29,010
Take me, death!

75
00:14:29,010 --> 00:14:32,260
Take me to Romeo.

76
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:37,990
Let's make you into a movie star.

77
00:14:37,990 --> 00:14:40,620
You might win an Academy Award.

78
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:44,230
When did you get here? You said it'd take 40 minutes.

79
00:14:44,230 --> 00:14:48,610
I think it's time you made your debut.

80
00:14:48,610 --> 00:14:51,030
Let's go to the studio. I'll be your manager.

81
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:56,330
A customer came to buy a laundry machine
and took the catalogue.

82
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:58,790
Stop fooling around and do your job!

83
00:14:58,790 --> 00:15:00,510
I'm leaving.

84
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:03,270
How long will your waste
your life as Yun's coordinator?

85
00:15:03,270 --> 00:15:05,740
I think you have the potential to be great.

86
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:08,140
I'm not saying that just because you're my sister.

87
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:11,350
You wouldn't be as good as Kang Min, but you...

88
00:15:11,350 --> 00:15:16,060
I know myself better than you. Mind your own business.

89
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:19,970
You know how hard it was for me to
get you this position, right?

90
00:15:19,970 --> 00:15:21,740
Better not get fired again.

91
00:15:25,890 --> 00:15:27,680
Yes?

92
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:30,490
Yun?

93
00:15:31,770 --> 00:15:34,450
Okay. I'll be there soon.

94
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:36,740
What did Yun do now?

95
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:40,540
You poor thing. You can't ever catch a break!

96
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:41,850
I got to go! See you later!

97
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:44,620
Okay, go. Go. Go.

98
00:15:45,830 --> 00:15:48,990
I did something bad, too...

99
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:51,990
They told me today was my last day...

100
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:54,280
My dumb boss...

101
00:15:56,950 --> 00:16:00,030
Wow. He's hot.

102
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,830
If he had money too, I'd marry him in a heartbeat!

103
00:16:03,830 --> 00:16:05,670
Wow, he's so good looking.

104
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:09,510
Cha Muhyeok. Is it true that you were adopted?

105
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:11,450
[Danny Anderson (Cha Muhyeok, 27)]
Yup.

106
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:18,060
You must have few memories
of your mother and of Korea.

107
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:21,610
I don' 'member nothing.

108
00:16:21,610 --> 00:16:26,550
Please pardon Muhyeok.
He's good at Korean,

109
00:16:26,550 --> 00:16:33,140
but he hasn't learned proper Korean.
I hope no one takes offense.

110
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:35,270
Yes, let's bring Cha Muhyeok on stage. Please come up.

111
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:38,090
Cha Muhyeok. Please come here.

112
00:16:38,090 --> 00:16:39,640
Please join us up here.

113
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:46,240
Tell us something that might help us find your family.

114
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:51,010
Do you have anything that was given
to you before you were adopted?

115
00:16:56,650 --> 00:17:02,540
We're airing live right now.

116
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:04,460
This show is live.

117
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:08,530
Excuse me, Cha Muhyeok...

118
00:17:10,810 --> 00:17:14,040
This must be a necklace with a story.

119
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:18,500
So is this what you had when you were adopted?

120
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,700
Yup.

121
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:24,660
When and how did you get it?

122
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:26,110
I dunno.

123
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:29,630
Can you please hold it up to the camera?

124
00:17:29,630 --> 00:17:32,850
That necklace is pretty.

125
00:17:32,850 --> 00:17:37,270
Where did I see that?
It doesn't seem like a necklace from Korea.

126
00:17:38,030 --> 00:17:42,730
Can you get out and ask the lady
where she got that necklace?

127
00:17:43,890 --> 00:17:45,940
Hello?

128
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:48,540
Can you go ask?

129
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:51,480
Yes, yes, ma'am.

130
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:04,000
Is that platinum or silver?

131
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,600
It's quite unique.

132
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,770
It's got ring with a string tied to it.

133
00:18:08,770 --> 00:18:12,290
Time to put on some pants...

134
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:19,680
It says, "Together."

135
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:24,540
It's written in Korean. It seems very important.

136
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:31,510
Hey! Change it back!

137
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:37,380
We have to keep watching so we can find your family.

138
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,680
No! I want to watch cartoons!

139
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:45,690
Wait a second. Let me just watch a minute of it.

140
00:18:45,690 --> 00:18:47,400
No!

141
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:52,720
Mom!

142
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:55,170
I'm going to watch cartoons!

143
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,750
["Forever"]

144
00:19:06,190 --> 00:19:08,720
Turn it back to the cartoons, Kim Galchi!

145
00:20:30,630 --> 00:20:31,940
Eunchae!

146
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:33,200
Yun!

147
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,360
He read this, and disappeared
in the middle of rehearsal.

148
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:37,280
What are we going to do?

149
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:43,100
I'll find him.

150
00:22:06,840 --> 00:22:09,280
Here's a napkin.

151
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:13,300
No. I'm going to ask my mom
to clean it when I meet her.

152
00:22:26,870 --> 00:22:29,400
"A woman is..."

153
00:22:31,090 --> 00:22:35,610
"Is... Is..."

154
00:22:35,610 --> 00:22:37,335
["That time of the month!"
Clean women's pads! Feels great!]

155
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:41,900
"Is long."

156
00:22:48,790 --> 00:22:52,620
"To a woman... It is..."

157
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:56,110
"P... Pad."

158
00:22:56,110 --> 00:23:00,660
You're super dumb.
How can you not know how to read that?

159
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:03,820
Oh, my!

160
00:23:05,010 --> 00:23:07,730
How dare you hit my kid!

161
00:23:09,270 --> 00:23:14,140
What a strange man. Are you okay?

162
00:23:14,140 --> 00:23:15,950
Oh, a pad...

163
00:23:15,950 --> 00:23:17,550
Pad.

164
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:18,920
Pad.

165
00:23:21,390 --> 00:23:24,200
"Feels..."

166
00:23:26,140 --> 00:23:28,930
"Feels great."

167
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:53,360
I love you.

168
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:56,770
You know you're the only one I love, right?

169
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:02,140
Cut! Okay! Next scene.

170
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:18,160
What the heck is that? Go check it out.

171
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:28,090
We're in the middle of filming! Can you keep it down?

172
00:24:28,090 --> 00:24:31,140
Come on! Please!

173
00:24:32,070 --> 00:24:34,780
Are you crazy?

174
00:24:34,780 --> 00:24:37,980
Hey! Don't you see we're filming?

175
00:24:37,980 --> 00:24:40,020
Sorry!

176
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:42,560
I'll take care of it.

177
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:45,230
Just go. Leave it to me.

178
00:24:45,230 --> 00:24:46,620
I'm sorry!

179
00:24:56,230 --> 00:24:57,550
Yun!

180
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:02,410
It's me! Open the door!

181
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:07,300
Yun, please don't do this.

182
00:25:10,890 --> 00:25:13,280
Please! Please don't do this.

183
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:16,410
What are you going to do if reporters see this?

184
00:25:18,700 --> 00:25:23,990
I don't get it. I seriously don't understand that girl.

185
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:26,910
I'm going nuts!

186
00:25:27,510 --> 00:25:29,590
I'm gonna die!

187
00:26:07,574 --> 00:26:09,720
Am I your servant?

188
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:12,570
"Am I your servant?"

189
00:26:12,570 --> 00:26:15,120
Do you want to die?

190
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:17,190
"Do you want to die?"

191
00:26:25,860 --> 00:26:27,190
Studio?

192
00:26:28,790 --> 00:26:30,090
Director?

193
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:34,670
Yeah.

194
00:26:36,210 --> 00:26:37,550
Where?

195
00:26:44,330 --> 00:26:45,730
Cha Muhyeok.

196
00:26:46,660 --> 00:26:49,980
Nice to meet you. Let's go.

197
00:26:51,100 --> 00:26:56,190
That doesn't taste good.

198
00:26:57,260 --> 00:26:59,120
No, I want to drink this.

199
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:01,950
Mom, you ordered that one. I ordered the cola.

200
00:27:01,950 --> 00:27:03,520
No, I ordered the cola. Give me it.

201
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:06,110
That little boy called us after watching the show.

202
00:27:06,110 --> 00:27:10,270
He told us that his mother has
the same exact same necklace.

203
00:27:10,270 --> 00:27:12,260
- Give it!
- No!

204
00:27:12,260 --> 00:27:15,150
- It's mine!
- Give it! Mine!

205
00:27:15,150 --> 00:27:16,770
Give it! It's mine!

206
00:27:16,770 --> 00:27:18,150
No! I want it!

207
00:27:18,150 --> 00:27:21,900
Give it! I want the cola!

208
00:27:25,090 --> 00:27:28,050
Mine! I want it!

209
00:27:28,050 --> 00:27:29,520
No, I was drinking it!

210
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:30,940
Give it!

211
00:27:35,525 --> 00:27:38,767
[Together Forever]

212
00:28:26,670 --> 00:28:30,330
She's like this because she was
in a car accident a long time ago.

213
00:28:32,870 --> 00:28:35,240
At age seven, a grandpa told me

214
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:39,500
she got hit by a truck in front
of the orphanage and hurt her head.

215
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:54,530
Read it.

216
00:28:57,470 --> 00:29:00,270
Read what's written in your ring.

217
00:29:11,140 --> 00:29:12,700
Don't know.

218
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:19,210
I don't know.

219
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:31,110
Can't your mother read?

220
00:29:32,510 --> 00:29:34,280
Is your mom an illiterate retard?

221
00:29:34,280 --> 00:29:35,790
She's not retarded.

222
00:29:35,790 --> 00:29:38,540
If she can't read at her age, how is she not retarded?

223
00:29:38,540 --> 00:29:40,650
It's because she hasn't learned all of her letters yet.

224
00:29:40,650 --> 00:29:44,400
She can read up to the seventh letter.

225
00:29:49,310 --> 00:29:51,180
What does it say?

226
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:57,280
Forever.

227
00:29:57,280 --> 00:29:58,810
Forever?

228
00:30:02,430 --> 00:30:04,120
Forever.

229
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:06,170
You can't read, either?

230
00:30:06,170 --> 00:30:09,200
There are some words I can, and some words I can't.

231
00:30:12,940 --> 00:30:15,390
But I'm not stupid.

232
00:30:15,390 --> 00:30:19,780
Compared to your mom, I'm 1,000 times smarter!

233
00:30:25,170 --> 00:30:28,670
"Forever... Together..."

234
00:30:50,230 --> 00:30:54,110
Do you know me?

235
00:30:56,960 --> 00:31:00,450
Who are you?

236
00:31:03,420 --> 00:31:05,110
Who are you?

237
00:31:18,650 --> 00:31:20,520
I'm Seo-kyeong.

238
00:31:24,130 --> 00:31:28,260
Yun Seo-kyeong.

239
00:32:25,850 --> 00:32:28,530
Eunchae, let's go home and make some spicy rice cakes.

240
00:32:29,450 --> 00:32:30,590
Okay.

241
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:45,880
I'll forget her.

242
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:51,200
Minju. From now on,
I'll completely erase her from my mind.

243
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:54,970
Without leaving a single trace.
I'm going to completely delete her.

244
00:32:54,970 --> 00:32:57,260
Goodbye, Kang Minju.

245
00:32:57,260 --> 00:33:01,360
It's goodbye forever!

246
00:33:04,270 --> 00:33:06,960
- Yun.
- What?

247
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:08,630
Don't lie.

248
00:33:40,590 --> 00:33:42,950
Grab a taxi and go home.

249
00:33:45,070 --> 00:33:48,080
I want to talk to Minju alone.

250
00:33:48,080 --> 00:33:51,550
I want to talk her alone. Go home.

251
00:33:55,130 --> 00:33:57,070
You have cab fare, right?

252
00:33:57,070 --> 00:33:58,340
Yes.

253
00:34:03,390 --> 00:34:06,270
I'm going to go get drunk. Will you wait here?

254
00:34:06,940 --> 00:34:10,950
I'll take a shot, come back,
and do something about Minju.

255
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:18,130
I'll tell her not to make you sad.
I'll knock some sense into her.

256
00:34:19,590 --> 00:34:23,830
Or I'll break her legs so that
she can't meet anyone else.

257
00:34:25,550 --> 00:34:28,580
Yeah. She's got it coming!

258
00:34:28,580 --> 00:34:30,280
Wait a second, I'll be back.

259
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:32,380
Don't lay a finger on her.

260
00:34:37,310 --> 00:34:39,360
It's not Minju's fault.

261
00:34:41,680 --> 00:34:43,790
She warned me.

262
00:34:45,900 --> 00:34:48,060
I'm the crazy one.

263
00:35:00,970 --> 00:35:02,410
Yun!

264
00:35:04,210 --> 00:35:05,720
Kang Minju!

265
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:10,970
I'll wait.

266
00:35:10,970 --> 00:35:12,600
- Get rid of him, and come to me.
- Hey!

267
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:16,570
